<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>CV Template</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <h1 style="font-size: 24pt; font-weight: bold;">Claude Steele Short Bio</h1>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
    <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span> is an American social psychologist and a Professor of Psychology at <span data-field="employer.name">{{ employer.name }}</span>.
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
    He is best known for his work on stereotype threat and its application to minority student academic performance. His earlier work dealt with research on the self (e.g., self-image, self-affirmation) as well as the role of self-regulation in addictive behaviors. In <span data-field="publication.title">{{ publication.title }}</span>, he released his book, <span data-field="publication.title">{{ publication.title }}</span>, summarizing years of research on stereotype threat and the underperformance of minority students in higher education.
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
    He holds a B.A. in Psychology from <span data-field="education.institution_ba">{{ education.institution_ba }}</span>, an M.A. in Social Psychology from <span data-field="education.institution_ma">{{ education.institution_ma }}</span>, and a Ph.D. in Social Psychology and Statistical Psychology from <span data-field="education.institution_phd">{{ education.institution_phd }}</span>.
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
    He is elected to the <span data-field="honor.award_1">{{ honor.award_1 }}</span>, the <span data-field="honor.award_2">{{ honor.award_2 }}</span>, the <span data-field="honor.award_3">{{ honor.award_3 }}</span>, and the <span data-field="honor.award_4">{{ honor.award_4 }}</span>.
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
    He currently serves as a trustee of the <span data-field="organization.trustee_1">{{ organization.trustee_1 }}</span> and the <span data-field="organization.trustee_2">{{ organization.trustee_2 }}</span>, and as a Fellow for both the <span data-field="organization.fellowship_1">{{ organization.fellowship_1 }}</span> and the <span data-field="organization.fellowship_2">{{ organization.fellowship_2 }}</span>.
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
    He has served in several major academic leadership positions as the <span data-field="position.role_1">{{ position.role_1 }}</span> and Provost at <span data-field="employer.name">{{ employer.name }}</span>, the <span data-field="position.role_2">{{ position.role_2 }}</span> for the School of Education at <span data-field="employer.name">{{ employer.name }}</span>, and as the <span data-field="position.role_3">{{ position.role_3 }}</span> of <span data-field="employer.name">{{ employer.name }}</span>. Past roles also include serving as the President of the Society for Personality and Social Psychology, President of the Western Psychological Association, a member of the Board of Directors American Psychological Society.
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
    <span data-field="summary.education_1">{{ summary.education_1 }}</span>
  </p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: left; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <p style="font-weight: bold;">Contact:</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">
      <span data-field="contact.name">{{ contact.name }}</span><br>
      <span data-field="contact.title">{{ contact.title }}</span><br>
      <span data-field="contact.affiliation">{{ contact.affiliation }}</span><br>
      <span data-field="contact.address_line_1">{{ contact.address_line_1 }}</span><br>
      <span data-field="contact.address_line_2">{{ contact.address_line_2 }}</span><br>
      Email: <span data-field="contact.email">{{ contact.email }}</span>
    </p>
  </div>
  <div style="text-align: right; margin-top: 50px;">
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">Phone: <span data-field="phone_number">{{ phone_number }}</span></p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">Assistant: <span data-field="assistant_name">{{ assistant_name }}</span>, <span data-field="assistant_email">{{ assistant_email }}</span>, <span data-field="assistant_phone">{{ assistant_phone }}</span></p>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>